From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: ignore the no-11ax mark Qualcomm dropped from its regdb

ath11k is a self-managed wiphy: the PHY restrictions of a country come
from the firmware, in the phybitmap of its regulatory event. Qualcomm's
regulatory database marked Belarus, Russia and Ukraine
REGULATORY_PHYMODE_NO11AX in June 2020. ath11k turns that into
NL80211_RRF_NO_HE on every rule, and cfg80211 then refuses a beacon with
an HE Operation element (-EOPNOTSUPP). With country RU and any HE htmode,
on either band, the AP does not start:

  hostapd: Failed to set beacon parameters
  hostapd: phy0-ap0: AP-DISABLED

while US, with the same modules, works (openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2 #57).

Qualcomm took the mark off again: regulatory database v35, of June 2021,
says "Add 11ax support for Russia & Ukraine", and v37, of November 2021,
drops it for Belarus. WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1-01744, built in August 2022 and the
newest firmware known for IPQ5018/QCN6122, still behaves as before them:
on this board, RU has NO-HE on every rule of both radios. Annex 2 of
Russia's GKRCh decision 07-20-03-001 sets limits for these bands by
modulation and power, and names no Wi-Fi standard.

Ignore NO11AX for these three countries. Their channels and power limits
stay the firmware's. Stations on them also stop being downgraded to VHT;
mesh never was, because mac80211 doesn't check the flag for it.

Tested on this board, with the image installed to NAND: on RU, BY and UA
an AP in an HE mode starts on both radios, with no NO-HE rules and HE in
the beacons a receiver could hear, and on RU a station passes traffic at
HE-MCS rates to an HE AP on both bands, with no firmware errors. An HE
client on such an AP has not been tested (docs/regulatory-ru-he.md).
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
@@ -363,9 +363,28 @@ static u32 ath11k_map_fw_reg_flags(u16 reg_flags)
 	return flags;
 }
 
-static u32 ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(u32 phy_flags)
+/* Countries where the firmware's built-in regulatory database appears to still
+ * forbid 802.11ax (NO11AX in the event's phybitmap), although Qualcomm's own
+ * database has dropped that. The database is compiled into the Q6 image, so it
+ * lags: database v35 of June 2021 says "Add 11ax support for Russia & Ukraine",
+ * v37 of November 2021 drops the mark for Belarus, and WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1-01744,
+ * from August 2022, behaves as before them.
+ */
+static const char ath11k_reg_fw_he_allowed[][3] = {
+	"BY",
+	"RU",
+	"UA",
+};
+
+static u32 ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(const struct cur_regulatory_info *reg_info)
 {
+	u32 phy_flags = reg_info->phybitmap;
 	u32 flags = 0;
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ath11k_reg_fw_he_allowed); i++)
+		if (!memcmp(ath11k_reg_fw_he_allowed[i], reg_info->alpha2, 2))
+			phy_flags &= ~ATH11K_REG_PHY_BITMAP_NO11AX;
 
 	if (phy_flags & ATH11K_REG_PHY_BITMAP_NO11AX)
 		flags |= NL80211_RRF_NO_HE;
@@ -567,7 +586,7 @@ static u8 ath11k_reg_add_fw_gaps(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 				       gap->start_freq, gap->end_freq,
 				       gap->max_bw, 0, gap->reg_power, 0,
 				       NL80211_RRF_AUTO_BW | gap->flags |
-				       ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(reg_info->phybitmap));
+				       ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(reg_info));
 		n_rules++;
 
 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_REG,
@@ -686,7 +705,7 @@ ath11k_reg_build_regd(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 		}
 
 		flags |= ath11k_map_fw_reg_flags(reg_rule->flags);
-		flags |= ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(reg_info->phybitmap);
+		flags |= ath11k_map_fw_phy_flags(reg_info);
 
 		ath11k_reg_update_rule(new_regd->reg_rules + i,
 				       reg_rule->start_freq,
